From 096bdf7b529284b75d360b8c12edae249d08a1d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:18:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a press through a scroll the app made on iOS

A press inside a scroll view was canceled on every topScroll, so a list
that scrolled itself under a finger at rest took the touch away: a chat
following a streaming reply with scrollToEnd never fired longPress on a
message. cancelPressForScroll assumed a programmatic scroll has no press
to cancel, but a finger can be down through one.

iOS marks such a scroll. RCTScrollViewComponentView sets
responderIgnoreScroll from !_isUserTriggeredScrolling, and React Native's
responder leaves a marked scroll out of a transfer. The engine now passes
a marked topScroll over on Apple's platforms.

Android sets the field on every scroll, the finger's included, so it is
not read there and a scroll under a finger cancels as before. A drag that
begins cancels on every platform.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
